{% doc %}
  @prompt
    add relevant Faq section with all the below faqs
    
    1) Where do you ship?
    
    We ship domestically and internationally where carriers support delivery. Available destinations and shipping options appear at checkout based on your address.
    
    2) How long does it take to make and ship my merch?
    
    Most merch is made to order. Production typically takes a few business days before it ships, and then shipping time depends on your location and the method you choose at checkout.
    
    3) Will I get tracking?
    
    Yes—once your order ships, you’ll receive a shipping confirmation with tracking details.
    
    4) Can I change or cancel my order after I place it?
    
    If you need to change a size, color, address, or cancel, contact us ASAP. Once an order enters production, changes may not be possible because items are made to order.
    
    5) How do I choose the right size?
    
    Use the size chart on each product page and compare it to a similar item you already own (lay it flat and measure). If you’re between sizes, sizing up usually gives a more relaxed fit—especially for hoodies.
    
    6) What if my item doesn’t fit—can I exchange it?
    
    If your item doesn’t fit, reach out and we’ll help you find the best option. Because many items are made to order, exchanges may depend on the item and condition. (Tip: double-check size charts before ordering—size uncertainty is one of the biggest reasons apparel gets returned.)
    
    7) What’s your return policy?
    
    If something arrives misprinted, damaged, or defective, contact us with photos and we’ll make it right. Claims for print defects/damage are commonly handled within a defined window after delivery (often 30 days).
    
    8) What if my order arrives damaged or the print looks wrong?
    
    Send us a message with your order number and clear photos of the issue. If it’s damaged, defective, or misprinted, we’ll coordinate a replacement or resolution according to the fulfillment partner’s claim window and process.
    
    9) What if my package is marked “delivered” but I don’t have it?
    
    First, check around your delivery location (mailroom, neighbors, front desk) and contact the carrier. If you still can’t locate it, message us and we’ll help you troubleshoot next steps.
    
    10) Do you restock items?
    
    Some drops are limited and may not restock. If something sells out, the best move is to join the waitlist / email list (or check back on the product page).
    
    11) Are these items printed on demand?
    
    Many modern merch stores use on-demand production so items are created after purchase rather than sitting in a warehouse. This helps reduce overproduction and keeps drops flexible (but it also means order changes are time-sensitive).
    
    12) Will the packaging show another company’s branding?
    
    If your merch is fulfilled through a white-label production partner, packaging is typically unbranded from the printer’s side (i.e., it doesn’t advertise the printer).
    
    13) Can I place a bulk order for an event or team?
    
    Yes—bulk orders are possible depending on the product. Send what you need (quantities, sizes, deadline, shipping location) and we’ll confirm pricing and timelines.
    
    14) Do you offer wholesale or collaborations?
    
    We’re open to collaborations that fit Ukiyo’s aesthetic and values. Reach out with your concept, audience, and what you’re envisioning.
    
    15) How do I contact support?
    
    Email or use the site contact form with your order number and a quick description. If there’s an issue, include photos—this speeds up resolution.
{% enddoc %}
{% assign ai_gen_id = block.id | replace: '_', '' | downcase %}

{% style %}
  .ai-faq-section-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: block;
    width: {{ block.settings.desktop_width_percent }}%;
    max-width: 100%;
    padding: {{ block.settings.section_padding }}px 20px;
    background-color: {{ block.settings.background_color }};
    color: {{ block.settings.text_color }};
  }

  .ai-faq-container-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-width: {{ block.settings.max_width }}px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .ai-faq-header-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    text-align: {{ block.settings.heading_alignment }};
    margin-bottom: {{ block.settings.heading_spacing }}px;
  }

  .ai-faq-heading-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.heading_size }}px;
    color: {{ block.settings.heading_color }};
    margin: 0 0 12px 0;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .ai-faq-subheading-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.subheading_size }}px;
    color: {{ block.settings.subheading_color }};
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ai-faq-list-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: {{ block.settings.item_spacing }}px;
  }

  .ai-faq-item-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    border: 1px solid {{ block.settings.border_color }};
    border-radius: {{ block.settings.border_radius }}px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background-color: {{ block.settings.item_background }};
  }

  .ai-faq-question-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    width: 100%;
    padding: {{ block.settings.question_padding }}px;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    text-align: left;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    color: {{ block.settings.question_color }};
    font-size: {{ block.settings.question_size }}px;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: background-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .ai-faq-question-{{ ai_gen_id }}:hover {
    background-color: {{ block.settings.question_hover_bg }};
  }

  .ai-faq-question-text-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    flex: 1;
  }

  .ai-faq-icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
    color: {{ block.settings.icon_color }};
  }

  .ai-faq-item-{{ ai_gen_id }}.active .ai-faq-icon-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .ai-faq-answer-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: max-height 0.3s ease, padding 0.3s ease;
  }

  .ai-faq-item-{{ ai_gen_id }}.active .ai-faq-answer-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-height: 1000px;
    padding: 0 {{ block.settings.question_padding }}px {{ block.settings.question_padding }}px;
  }

  .ai-faq-answer-content-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.answer_size }}px;
    color: {{ block.settings.answer_color }};
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .ai-faq-section-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      padding: {{ block.settings.section_padding | times: 0.6 }}px 16px;
    }

    .ai-faq-heading-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.heading_size | times: 0.8 }}px;
    }

    .ai-faq-subheading-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.subheading_size | times: 0.9 }}px;
    }

    .ai-faq-question-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.question_size | times: 0.9 }}px;
      padding: {{ block.settings.question_padding | times: 0.8 }}px;
    }

    .ai-faq-answer-content-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.answer_size | times: 0.9 }}px;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

